WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:17,020
Does anyone do blood transfusions with blood from someone who has beaten ovarian cancer?

00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:23,020
Nope, that does not happen. That would be legally in the United States.

00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:32,020
And if the idea, I think this person is getting at is that if somebody beat a specific type of cancer,

00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:44,020
would there be any chemicals, chemokines in the blood, antibodies in the blood that would help another person with that same type of cancer?

00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:55,020
Well, your body doesn't kill cancer by developing antibodies to the cancer, so that wouldn't be a factor at all.

00:00:55,020 --> 00:01:06,020
I think there'd be zero benefit to get to receive blood from somebody who had a disease like ovarian cancer in overcame it.

00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:13,020
If you got blood from somebody that had an overcame, like, let's say, a bacterial infection,

00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:20,020
you received their blood, you'd be receiving possible antibodies to that bacteria, but not to a cancer.

